# ulsrcmap.libs -- declared source for a LINK-TIME LIBRARY (an archive named
# on a link line), keyed by the archive's basename.
#
# ulsrcmap.py's expand() can name an archive's members only by finding, in
# THIS build's own compile record, an object it logged beside/below the
# archive -- and an archive nobody recompiled this run (already up to date)
# leaves no such record.  The search that stands in for one then widens past
# the archive's own directory and can attribute an unrelated library's
# objects to it instead: os/net/libsocket.a sits directly in a top-level
# source directory, so its widest step is "below net's parent", which is
# every object this build logged ANYWHERE in the tree.  A hand-checked row
# here is trusted ahead of that search, because it cannot go stale silently
# (a moved or renamed source drops out at read time, same as ulsrcmap.extra)
# and it cannot mis-attribute -- the failure mode the search cannot rule out.
#
# Checked against every archive a link line named as of #<task370b>: MGR's
# client library and the toolchain's curses/libterm resolve correctly through
# the compile record today (their objects log beside or below them) and are
# not listed here on purpose -- a row would just be a second, unreviewed copy
# of a fact the record already states correctly.
#
# Same format as ulsrcmap.extra: `<archive-basename> <TAB> <source path>...',
# paths relative to os/, a path may be a file or a directory, `#' comments.
# A PATH THIS TREE DOES NOT HOLD is one another repository publishes: it is
# carried unconditionally for the programs that link the archive, and the
# consumer resolves it across the whole search path -- the same rule that puts
# the C library's own source in the package of everything linked against it.
#
# libsocket.a -- os/net/Makefile's own member list (libsocket.o gethostby.o
# netdb.o $(CHAN) $(RESOLV) $(RCMD)); CHAN and rawsys.s are what every net
# client links for its syscall gate, RESOLV is the DNS resolver gethostby.o
# calls into, RCMD is the r-commands' shared rcmd()/iruserok().
libsocket.a	net/libsocket.c net/gethostby.c net/netdb.c net/inet_chan.c net/rawsys.s net/rcmd.c net/ruserok.c net/resolv

# libhrgfx.a and libvellum.a -- the hi-res rendering engine and Vellum's drawing
# model, hr/Makefile's own member lists (HRGFX_ASM HRGFX_C; VELLIBOBJ).  Both
# archives stand in hostbuild/build/obj/hrgui, where the objects of every
# window-system program are logged below them, so the search would hand each
# client the whole desktop's sources; each archive is one source directory.
libhrgfx.a	hr/gfx
libvellum.a	hr/lib/vellum

# libm-z8001.a and libmisc-z8001.a -- the maths library and the small support
# library, built by the TOOLCHAIN repository from src/libm and src/libmisc.
# Every program that calls sin(), pow() or the long-arithmetic helpers links
# one of them, and its complete corresponding source includes theirs.  libm.a
# is the same archive under the name hr/Makefile stages it as.
libm-z8001.a	src/libm
libm.a	src/libm
libmisc-z8001.a	src/libmisc
